  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d8f03af1-56ac-4a4a-aee1-0911619dfbd8-9895034.PNG\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 130px;\" /></p><p>For the second case when body is moving with constant velocity, we can write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Now this velocity if the final velocity for the first case, therefore</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Hence, required force will be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p>",
